---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="About"
  description="Why independent property investment verification should exist, why conflicts of interest matter, and why evidence changes the outcome for the buyer."
  path="/about"
>
  <section class="hero-simple">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
      <h1>Why independent verification exists.</h1>
      <p class="hero-sub text-muted">Every party in a typical property transaction is paid when the deal closes. I'm the exception.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <p class="lead">In most cross-border property transactions, everyone advising the buyer has an interest in the transaction happening.</p>
      <p class="text-muted">
        The developer is selling inventory. The broker earns commission on completion, regardless of whether the price is fair. The
        relocation consultant is often paid a referral fee by the agent they introduce. Even a well-intentioned advisor operating inside
        that structure is, at some level, incentivised toward "yes."
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted">
        None of this makes any of those parties dishonest. It means their incentives are not aligned with the single question that
        actually matters to the buyer: <em>is this specific acquisition, at this specific price, a good investment?</em>
      </p>

      <h2 class="section-h2">A different structure</h2>
      <p class="text-muted">
        I don't sell property, broker transactions, or introduce buyers to sellers. I'm commissioned to answer one question,
        independent of whether the answer helps the transaction close, using a fixed process I call the Lana Method. I hold
        no position, take no commission, and have no relationship with the developer, the seller, or the broker on any deal I review.
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted">
        This is a structural choice, not a marketing claim. It is also why some reviews conclude with a recommendation to walk
        away — an outcome no party paid on commission has an incentive to reach.
      </p>

      <h2 class="section-h2">Who this is for</h2>
      <p class="text-muted">
        Family offices allocating across jurisdictions. International investors and second-home buyers without an in-house underwriting
        function. Buyer's agents who want independent evidence they can hand to a client without absorbing the underwriting risk
        themselves. Private banks assessing collateral. Law firms who want financial verification to sit alongside their own legal
        due diligence.
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted">
        I'm not a fit for institutional funds with in-house appraisal teams, or for anyone looking for deal sourcing, brokerage,
        or introductions — that's a different business, deliberately not this one.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--stone">
    <div class="container founder-row">
      <div class="founder-portrait" aria-hidden="true">
        <span>SO</span>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Background</span>
        <h2 class="founder-name">Svetlana (Lana) Olenchuk</h2>
        <p class="text-muted founder-bio">
          I built the Lana Method on a simple premise: a property investment decision deserves the same independent
          scrutiny as any other significant capital allocation, delivered by someone with no stake in whether the transaction
          closes. I work across UAE, Cyprus, the UK, continental Europe, and the US, reviewing acquisitions before capital
          is committed.
        </p>
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/svetlana-olenchuk-b48304b1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="founder-linkedin">Connect on LinkedIn ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta-section">
    <div class="container cta-inner">
      <div>
        <h2>Have a deal to verify?</h2>
        <p class="text-muted">I'll tell you what the evidence says — even when that means telling you not to buy.</p>
      </div>
      <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Commission a Review</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero-simple { padding: 64px 0 48px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .hero-simple h1 { font-size: clamp(30px, 4.5vw, 46px); margin: 16px 0 18px; max-width: 20ch; }
  .hero-sub { font-size: 16px; max-width: 56ch; line-height: 1.6; }

  .narrow { max-width: 700px; }
  .lead { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 24px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.4; margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .narrow p.text-muted { font-size: 15.5px; line-height: 1.75; margin-bottom: 18px; }
  .section-h2 { font-size: 22px; margin: 40px 0 16px; }

  .founder-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 140px 1fr; gap: 36px; align-items: start; }
  .founder-portrait { width: 140px; height: 140px; background: var(--navy); color: #fff; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 800; font-size: 32px; }
  .founder-name { font-size: 26px; margin: 14px 0 12px; }
  .founder-bio { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7; max-width: 60ch; }
  .founder-linkedin { display: inline-block; margin-top: 16px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 13px; color: var(--navy); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--navy); padding-bottom: 2px; }

  .cta-inner { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 24px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .cta-inner h2 { font-size: 24px; margin-bottom: 8px; }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .founder-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
